  "verdict": "With the source kept live (solid top skin) and equal occupancy (tree 150 cells = straight 150 cells, both covering 25/25 source cells), the 3D peak difference is -0.0011 C at Bi=1 and spans [-0.0011, -0.0011] C over Bi in {0, 1, 10} plus the isothermal-base limit; the sign is stable across the sweep. Rebuilding at grid 40 moves each difference by at most 2.0e-06 C. On a peak that the channels lower by 0.7940 C against the bare plate, |dT| is 0.14% of the cooling effect. Because occupancy AND source coverage are equalised by construction, this comparison cannot attribute the tie to coverage; what it does establish is that the tie survives the third dimension rather than being an artefact of the 2D reduction."
